659
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:25,656
<i>Please reflect on the mistakes
you have made</i>

660
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:28,201
<i>and discuss them amongst yourselves.</i>

661
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:31,036
<i>This time, it's Kahochi.</i>

662
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:33,414
- Okay.
- <i>Please go ahead.</i>

663
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:36,668
All right.

664
00:30:37,710 --> 00:30:38,877
I will tell my story.

665
00:30:38,878 --> 00:30:41,046
- You can do it.
- Good luck, do your best.

666
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:42,048
First of all,

667
00:30:43,258 --> 00:30:44,926
my father was very strict.

668
00:30:45,426 --> 00:30:49,012
Yeah, when I was in middle school,
he was very serious about curfews.

669
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:52,266
And I think that just made me
want to rebel even more.

670
00:30:52,267 --> 00:30:55,269
So pretty soon, I started
to get into all kinds of trouble.

671
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:57,981
And, like, I got arrested
for possession of marijuana.

672
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:03,570
My dad is a huge worrywart,
and we ended up getting into a fight.

673
00:31:04,988 --> 00:31:06,822
He told me to get out of the house,

674
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:09,409
so I left and ran away from home
for two months.

675
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:13,120
And then my mom told me
that my dad was worried about me,

676
00:31:13,121 --> 00:31:14,539
and that I should come home.

677
00:31:15,707 --> 00:31:18,417
But, like, I was still
getting into more trouble.

678
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:20,294
Then I finally went back.

679
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:23,965
At the time, my dad seemed
very apologetic about it, you know.

680
00:31:26,634 --> 00:31:28,428
I said I'm sorry for running away.

681
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:37,812
And then, like, at the time…

682
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:41,900
we talked it out with each other.

683
00:31:44,903 --> 00:31:47,321
I made him…

684
00:31:47,322 --> 00:31:50,491
…go through a lot, like,
with people at his work and everything.

685
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:52,618
Mmm.

686
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,953
He worried that people would think…

687
00:31:54,954 --> 00:31:56,247
<i>Oh, what's wrong?</i>

688
00:31:56,789 --> 00:32:00,876
When I got arrested by the police, like,
he didn't even yell at me.

689
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:02,503
He just scolded me quietly.

690
00:32:03,546 --> 00:32:04,881
Mmm.

691
00:32:06,674 --> 00:32:08,592
- <i>Look what she's doing.</i>
- Thanks.

692
00:32:08,593 --> 00:32:10,385
<i>That's nice of her. Yeah.</i>

693
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:14,222
I know I'm still a burden on them,
and I'm, like, so sorry about that.

694
00:32:14,223 --> 00:32:17,936
I feel the most sorry
for my dad, honestly.

695
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:23,231
And then, when I was 16,
I had a boyfriend,

696
00:32:23,232 --> 00:32:25,735
I got pregnant and had a baby.

697
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:31,115
And we weren't married.
We broke up before I turned 18.

698
00:32:31,741 --> 00:32:35,369
I couldn't raise the baby on my own,
so my dad and my mom…

699
00:32:35,370 --> 00:32:37,497
I also have a younger brother and sister.

700
00:32:38,414 --> 00:32:39,415
They all…

701
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:41,876
help me out a lot.

702
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:45,463
My parents look after my child
while I go to work.

703
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:49,466
Do you ever think about
doing something for your parents?

704
00:32:49,467 --> 00:32:53,011
Yeah, I've been thinking that
since I was in middle school.

705
00:32:53,012 --> 00:32:54,806
Like, um…

706
00:32:55,848 --> 00:32:57,849
Wait a minute.

707
00:32:57,850 --> 00:32:58,976
That's a good joke.

708
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:01,770
It's cute, but…

709
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:04,524
I want to build a house,
just for my dad and mom.

710
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:08,236
I've been thinking about it for a while.

711
00:33:09,904 --> 00:33:14,116
I started running a bar
when I was only 24 years old,

