00:44:21,575 --> 00:44:24,577
So, you know, I know I started
talking to you on the first day,

950
00:44:24,578 --> 00:44:26,163
and every day since then.

951
00:44:26,705 --> 00:44:29,499
I trust that you see me for who I am.

952
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:31,459
- And what I felt on the first day…
- Mmm-hmm?

953
00:44:31,460 --> 00:44:35,004
…I will do my best
to keep expressing that right to the end.

954
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:36,506
- Yeah.
- That's enough.

955
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:38,675
You lost, so just chill till we get back.

956
00:44:38,676 --> 00:44:40,552
- I did lose the race.
- So then…

957
00:44:41,095 --> 00:44:43,054
- Just the race.
- Wait, then we'll be back.

958
00:44:43,055 --> 00:44:44,138
That's it.

959
00:44:44,139 --> 00:44:47,100
I'm giving this to you too.
I want to lose track of time.

960
00:44:47,101 --> 00:44:48,184
- Okay.
- Here.

961
00:44:48,185 --> 00:44:50,020
- Thank you.
- We'll talk again tomorrow.

962
00:44:50,646 --> 00:44:53,439
- I'll be waiting.
- Yeah, me too.

963
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:54,942
Okay, I see.

964
00:44:55,734 --> 00:44:58,194
- See you, Mimi.
- So that's how it is.

965
00:44:58,195 --> 00:44:59,654
- See you.
- Sounds good.

966
00:44:59,655 --> 00:45:00,656
- Let's go.
- I'm off.

967
00:45:02,199 --> 00:45:03,200
Bye.

968
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:17,296
Wow, this is something.

969
00:45:17,297 --> 00:45:19,090
We can't even tell what it's like inside.

970
00:45:19,091 --> 00:45:20,174
No.

971
00:45:20,175 --> 00:45:22,386
Wow, it looks so luxurious.

972
00:45:23,929 --> 00:45:25,472
Oh, here it is.

973
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:32,478
- Oh, wow.
- What's it like?

974
00:45:32,479 --> 00:45:35,023
- It's so beautiful.
- Oh, wow, so stylish.

975
00:45:35,899 --> 00:45:36,900
So cool.

976
00:45:38,068 --> 00:45:40,945
Totally different
from the loud vibe at school.

977
00:45:40,946 --> 00:45:42,530
- Yeah.
- Loud. Chaotic, even.

978
00:45:42,531 --> 00:45:44,824
Oh, wow, check out this bathtub.

979
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:46,826
We bathe here?

980
00:45:46,827 --> 00:45:49,412
Such a distance from the bath
to the shower.

981
00:45:49,413 --> 00:45:51,081
Wow, but it's so beautiful.

982
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:56,170
- It's so nice.
- Hey, it's a pool.

983
00:45:58,213 --> 00:46:01,008
- Is it cold?
- Amazing. It has to be cold.

984
00:46:01,633 --> 00:46:03,134
- I bet is.
- Oh, it's warm.

985
00:46:03,135 --> 00:46:05,763
- Really? It is?
- Because it's cold outside.

986
00:46:06,555 --> 00:46:07,556
This is nice.

987
00:46:08,766 --> 00:46:10,641
- I want to sit.
- Let's sit.

988
00:46:10,642 --> 00:46:12,019
- Okay, cheers!
- Okay.

989
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:19,942
I was worried for a moment
about what was going to happen.

990
00:46:19,943 --> 00:46:20,944
Why?

991
00:46:21,445 --> 00:46:23,863
Well, I mean, in my mind,

992
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:26,407
- I could only think about being here.
- Hmm.

993
00:46:26,408 --> 00:46:27,576
- On this date.
- Mmm.

994
00:46:28,202 --> 00:46:31,454
So, like, I thought it would be so lame
if I couldn't go.

995
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:32,956
And yesterday, in the kitchen,

996
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:35,792
I said, "Let's go on an overnight date."

997
00:46:35,793 --> 00:46:38,169
- Mmm, you did say that.
- I said I was going to win.

998
00:46:38,170 --> 00:46:41,589
I thought it'd be so lame
if I made that bold claim and lost.

999
00:46:41,590 --> 00:46:43,633
Things with the girls are kind of tense.

1000
00:46:43,634 --> 00:46:45,843
It's not like
we're fighting over the guys,

1001
00:46:45,844 --> 00:46:48,387
but there's still some awkwardness
between us.

1002
00:46:48,388 --> 00:46:50,640
It's kind of tough. Do the guys have that?

1003
00:46:50,641 --> 00:46:52,016
- You don't, right?
- Hmm.

1004
00:46:52,017 --> 00:46:54,519
- We don't, but also, like…
- They're pretty chill.

1005
00:46:54,520 --> 00:46:56,896
For a while,
I thought that everyone was chill.

1006
00:46:56,897 --> 00:47:00,150
But I realized that wasn't the case
when you and I were leaving today.

1007
00:47:02,069 --> 00:47:04,696
<i>For real, I didn't like it.
I'm not happy about that at all.</i>

1008
00:47:05,280 --> 00:47:07,657
I mean, when we had a fair fight
in front of everyone,

1009
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:10,660
they said, "We fought like men,
so I will not go back on my word."

1010
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:13,080
We shook hands,
thanking each other for the race.

1011
00:47:13,664 --> 00:47:16,332
- And they came back again? It was weird.
- Yeah.

1012
00:47:16,333 --> 00:47:18,876
- If they were actually rooting for us…
- Mmm.

1013
00:47:18,877 --> 00:47:21,045
…they wouldn't have given you that stuff,

1014
00:47:21,046 --> 00:47:23,923
and try to use it as a tool
to wedge us a part.

1015
00:47:23,924 --> 00:47:25,132
Totally unnecessary.

1016
00:47:25,133 --> 00:47:26,843
Seriously. I would never do that.

1017
00:47:26,844 --> 00:47:29,637
If I lost, I'd would just go into my room,
and keep to myself.

1018
00:47:29,638 --> 00:47:30,847
- You know what I mean?
- Mmm-hmm.

1019
00:47:30,848 --> 00:47:31,974
It is what it is.

1020
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:34,768
So I think I'll talk about that
when I get back.

1021
00:47:35,394 --> 00:47:36,603
Okay, I see. Yeah.

1022
00:47:43,360 --> 00:47:47,614
<i>Now, it's time to get ready
for the locals' thank-you party.</i>

1023
00:47:48,740 --> 00:47:50,784
Okay, we'll work on the bench.

1024
00:47:51,451 --> 00:47:55,497
Oh, this is great.

1025
00:47:56,206 --> 00:47:59,876
<i>It was Rune's idea to make
this bench for the locals, remember that?</i>

1026
00:47:59,877 --> 00:48:01,712
- <i>Oh, yeah! I see, yeah.</i>
- <i>Oh, nice.</i>

1027
00:48:03,422 --> 00:48:05,173
- Once I start, I can't stop.
- It's hot.

1028
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:07,217
I need gloves.

1029
00:48:08,260 --> 00:48:11,888
Wow, that's nice. At this rate, we could
probably make three of these benches.

1030
00:48:11,889 --> 00:48:12,890
You bet we can.

1031
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:16,018
I wonder how far they've gotten.

1032
00:48:16,602 --> 00:48:18,270
- What do you mean?
- The overnight.

1033
00:48:20,439 --> 00:48:22,690
Honestly, I was about to cry
in that moment.

1034
00:48:22,691 --> 00:48:24,025
I was so frustrated.

1035
00:48:24,026 --> 00:48:26,403
I wish there was another chance
to go on a date.

1036
00:48:28,530 --> 00:48:29,907
This is excruciating.

1037
00:48:30,699 --> 00:48:33,577
Why would you say that
in front of Sharan, Tai-chan?

1038
00:48:34,411 --> 00:48:36,663
It's almost like he's doing it on purpose.

1039
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:38,415
Do I drink a lot?

1040
00:48:38,999 --> 00:48:41,042
- Do you think I drink a lot?
- I think you do.

1041
00:48:41,043 --> 00:48:42,376
- Hey.
- But I'm having fun.

1042
00:48:42,377 --> 00:48:45,004
Am I different
from the girls you've met so far?

1043
00:48:45,005 --> 00:48:46,839
- You probably drink the most.
- Oh, yeah?

1044
00:48:46,840 --> 00:48:48,216
- Yeah.
- I see.

1045
00:48:48,800 --> 00:48:50,761
- I'm not really interested in clothes.
- Mmm-hmm.

1046
00:48:51,887 --> 00:48:53,095
My mom was.

1047
00:48:53,096 --> 00:48:56,223
I mean, my mom is super interested
in clothes and fashion,

1048
00:48:56,224 --> 00:48:57,726
and what to wear, all that.

1049
00:48:59,269 --> 00:49:01,270
- So she buys all my clothes.
- Oh, nice.

1050
00:49:01,271 --> 00:49:04,982
I went through a lot of tough times
when I was young, because of my mom.

1051
00:49:04,983 --> 00:49:07,610
- Mmm-hmm.
- When I was in elementary school,

1052
00:49:07,611 --> 00:49:09,403
I would come home in the evening--

1053
00:49:09,404 --> 00:49:11,572
- No, no, in the afternoon.
- Mmm…

1054
00:49:11,573 --> 00:49:13,908
And at the time, I could never figure out

1055
00:49:13,909 --> 00:49:17,578
why she was always in such a terrible mood
when I got home.

1056
00:49:17,579 --> 00:49:20,665
I was like, "Why do I have to be
so careful around her?"

1057
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:23,919
Now that I work in nightlife, I understand
how hard it must have been for her.

1058
00:49:24,586 --> 00:49:26,004
I can understand that now.

1059
00:49:27,130 --> 00:49:30,383
We still fight, but I also depend on her
for a lot of things.

1060
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:31,467
Mmm.

1061
00:49:31,468 --> 00:49:33,804
Yeah. I love my mom.

1062
00:49:34,554 --> 00:49:37,431
- That's nice.
- I don't want to be like my mom, though.

1063
00:49:37,432 --> 00:49:39,351
I want to be an even more
attractive woman than her.

1064
00:49:40,477 --> 00:49:44,105
Since last year,
my job has finally settled down a bit,

1065
00:49:44,106 --> 00:49:47,316
so we can go on trips together,
and that kind of stuff.

1066
00:49:47,317 --> 00:49:51,153
And we're finally going to go
on our first overseas trip together soon.

1067
00:49:51,154 --> 00:49:52,322
- That'll be fun.
- That's nice.

1068
00:49:53,115 --> 00:49:54,116
You know, I just…

1069
00:49:55,242 --> 00:49:58,077
I love my mom. So much.

1070
00:49:58,078 --> 00:49:59,079
I really do.

1071
00:50:00,288 --> 00:50:01,289
Mmm.

1072
00:50:02,499 --> 00:50:06,502
Now that I'm an adult, I can understand
how hard she was working to raise me

1073
00:50:06,503 --> 00:50:08,295
while also working at night.

1074
00:50:08,296 --> 00:50:11,799
I think she wanted to enjoy being a woman,
and not just a mom.

1075
00:50:11,800 --> 00:50:13,843
Because she is more than just a mother.

1076
00:50:13,844 --> 00:50:16,638
The fact is,
I had clothes to wear, food to eat,

1077
00:50:17,139 --> 00:50:18,890
and I had a roof over my head.

1078
00:50:19,474 --> 00:50:22,643
The biggest thing is that
she sent me to a good school,

1079
00:50:22,644 --> 00:50:24,354
which costs a lot of money.

1080
00:50:25,105 --> 00:50:26,690
She did all that for me.

1081
00:50:27,649 --> 00:50:31,695
I realized as an adult that she worked
so hard to be able to take care of me.

1082
00:50:32,696 --> 00:50:34,573
That hit me pretty hard. I mean…

1083
00:50:35,907 --> 00:50:38,325
Back then, I thought it was kind of cool

1084
00:50:38,326 --> 00:50:41,704
to pretend not to understand things,
even if I actually did.

1085
00:50:41,705 --> 00:50:42,706
But now,

1086
00:50:43,373 --> 00:50:46,001
I think that what I did
was actually just lame.

1087
00:50:46,877 --> 00:50:48,586
The more I thought about it,

1088
00:50:48,587 --> 00:50:51,131
the more I realized
that I was a pretty lame kid.

1089
00:50:52,007 --> 00:50:53,008
Mmm.

1090
00:50:55,260 --> 00:50:58,137
- I wanted to win so bad.
- I wanted you to win too.

1091
00:50:58,138 --> 00:51:00,015
You know, if I had won today…

1092
00:51:00,724 --> 00:51:02,600
I'm just gonna say it.

1093
00:51:02,601 --> 00:51:03,602
Straight up.

1094
00:51:04,102 --> 00:51:06,354
- Come on, look at me.
- What is it?

1095
00:51:08,690 --> 00:51:09,900
I would have chosen you.

1096
00:51:11,526 --> 00:51:12,778
- Really?
- Yeah.

1097
00:51:13,361 --> 00:51:15,072
That makes me smile.

1098
00:51:15,655 --> 00:51:18,240
- You rooted for me? No way.
- Yeah, I did.

1099
00:51:18,241 --> 00:51:20,409
Yeah, I was like, "Yes!" in my heart.

1100
00:51:20,410 --> 00:51:21,702
- Oh, when I won?
- Yeah.

1101
00:51:21,703 --> 00:51:22,953
- The first round?
- Mmm.

1102
00:51:22,954 --> 00:51:24,872
But it was a close race.

1103
00:51:24,873 --> 00:51:27,041
- Did you see it? When I got it?
- I saw it.

1104
00:51:27,042 --> 00:51:28,460
Oh, you did?

1105
00:51:29,336 --> 00:51:32,047
I don't know how many years it's been
since I ran that hard.

1106
00:51:33,799 --> 00:51:36,092
- Was my running kind of weird?
- Not at all.

1107
00:51:36,093 --> 00:51:37,094
It wasn't?

1108
00:51:38,386 --> 00:51:40,721
Everything you do looks cool.

1109
00:51:40,722 --> 00:51:42,306
- <i>Oh, she said it!</i>
- <i>Cute.</i>

1110
00:51:42,307 --> 00:51:43,308
Really?

1111
00:51:44,351 --> 00:51:48,312
- <i>Oh, man! Kamaken is adorable.</i>
- <i>He's totally smitten.</i>

1112
00:51:48,313 --> 00:51:51,066
I feel like things have changed a lot
since we went on that date.

1113
00:51:51,733 --> 00:51:53,777
- Yeah, exactly.
- Yeah, yeah, for sure.

1114
00:51:54,653 --> 00:51:56,529
I think it's fun to talk with you,

1115
00:51:56,530 --> 00:51:58,657
and I feel like
I can be myself around you.

1116
00:51:59,366 --> 00:52:01,701
- Oh, really?
- Absolutely. For sure.

1117
00:52:03,161 --> 00:52:05,455
So when we were walking
on the beach earlier,

1118
00:52:06,832 --> 00:52:10,794
I was thinking to myself,
"If I go with anyone, it'll be Rinrin."

1119
00:52:19,177 --> 00:52:20,720
Hey, you're not talking at all today.

1120
00:52:21,596 --> 00:52:23,097
Rinrin.

1121
00:52:23,098 --> 00:52:25,225
<i>Look at those eyes. She's so cute!</i>

1122
00:52:27,686 --> 00:52:31,981
- My heart's fluttering all over the place.
- <i>So cute!</i>

1123
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:34,567
His face, his movement,
everything about him is cool.

1124
00:52:34,568 --> 00:52:35,569
I love it.

1125
00:52:39,489 --> 00:52:41,907
Rune, what about taking a bath?

1126
00:52:41,908 --> 00:52:44,202
- The bath?
- We need to bathe.

1127
00:52:45,078 --> 00:52:47,288
- Rune, you go first.
- Okay.

1128
00:52:47,289 --> 00:52:48,539
- Since I take so long.
- Okay.

1129
00:52:48,540 --> 00:52:49,957
- Yeah.
- Like, now?

1130
00:52:49,958 --> 00:52:51,876
That's better, right? If we do that,

1131
00:52:51,877 --> 00:52:55,337
I could take my makeup off
and drink later if we're going to.

1132
00:52:55,338 --> 00:52:57,424
- So let's take our baths now.
- I'll go take one.

1133
00:52:58,633 --> 00:53:00,802
<i>He's been pretty cool-headed
up till now, right?</i>

1134
00:53:08,310 --> 00:53:09,352
<i>What's happening?</i>

1135
00:53:28,038 --> 00:53:28,954
Dear Mimi,

1136
00:53:28,955 --> 00:53:31,207
In Part 1, I saw an overnight date
change everything.

1137
00:53:31,208 --> 00:53:33,417
I wanted to win and take you on a date,
but I failed.

1138
00:53:33,418 --> 00:53:36,086
Even though that dream is dead,
I'll work hard for both of us!

1139
00:53:36,087 --> 00:53:37,630
The distance and our ages don't matter.

1140
00:53:37,631 --> 00:53:39,048
I'll show you my love in my own way!

1141
00:53:39,049 --> 00:53:41,051
My writing sucks,
but my feelings are true. Taisei

1142
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:49,683
I received a letter and clothes
from Tai-chan.

1143
00:53:49,684 --> 00:53:53,020
Maru struggled to find something too,
and he handed me his watch.

1144
00:53:53,021 --> 00:53:56,399
Like, I think those gestures
had an impact on me.

1145
00:53:56,900 --> 00:53:57,901
Even when…

1146
00:53:58,735 --> 00:54:02,029
I was talking to Rune,
in the back of my mind,

1147
00:54:02,030 --> 00:54:05,699
it's not like they were there,
but I was thinking about the two of them.

1148
00:54:05,700 --> 00:54:07,910
And a part of me
felt kind of bad for them.

1149
00:54:07,911 --> 00:54:11,748
I wanted to focus, but my brain
was kind of all over the place.

1150
00:54:24,386 --> 00:54:28,597
So, like, Tai-chan gave me that letter
before we left, and I read it.

1151
00:54:28,598 --> 00:54:29,599
Mmm.

1152
00:54:30,141 --> 00:54:33,353
- I just wanted to let you know.
- Mmm. What did you think?

1153
00:54:33,979 --> 00:54:36,981
- Hmm, I thought it was cute.
- Mmm.

1154
00:54:36,982 --> 00:54:39,859
I can't help but think
that he's adorable. It's like…

1155
00:54:40,694 --> 00:54:43,195
I don't want to keep any secrets from you.

1156
00:54:43,196 --> 00:54:45,447
- So, you know, the day before…
- Mmm.

1157
00:54:45,448 --> 00:54:47,616
…it was when we all had

1158
00:54:47,617 --> 00:54:49,952
that one-on-one time
to talk with each other,

1159
00:54:49,953 --> 00:54:52,454
Maru told me
he was going to try hard for me,

1160
00:54:52,455 --> 00:54:54,666
and Tai-chan said he'd do his best too.

1161
00:54:55,417 --> 00:54:57,334
So, of course,
I was watching the tournament

1162
00:54:57,335 --> 00:54:59,420
- with all of that running through my mind.
- Mmm.

1163
00:54:59,421 --> 00:55:01,130
But in the end, I'd have no idea

1164
00:55:01,131 --> 00:55:02,966
if someone would choose me
until it happens.

1165
00:55:03,591 --> 00:55:05,467
They can say they'll choose me,

1166
00:55:05,468 --> 00:55:07,511
- but I don't know for sure.
- Mmm.

1167
00:55:07,512 --> 00:55:10,306
And I'm a pretty
skeptical person after all.

1168
00:55:10,307 --> 00:55:11,516
And, I don't know,

1169
00:55:12,142 --> 00:55:15,144
especially because of
this whole environment we're in,

1170
00:55:15,145 --> 00:55:17,646
where we have six girls, it's six and six.

1171
00:55:17,647 --> 00:55:19,148
I didn't want a guy to be thinking,

1172
00:55:19,149 --> 00:55:21,359
"I hope I end up
with the best of these six."

1173
00:55:21,943 --> 00:55:25,321
You're being very clear about things,
and about what you feel.

1174
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:28,198
And, like, I wasn't thinking I'd pick you

1175
00:55:28,199 --> 00:55:30,534
just because you were the best
out of the six.

1176
00:55:30,535 --> 00:55:31,828
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

1177
00:55:33,163 --> 00:55:35,664
- I thought you maybe felt that way.
- Honestly, I feel like…

1178
00:55:35,665 --> 00:55:37,624
Whether it was 6 girls or 100,

1179
00:55:37,625 --> 00:55:40,169
it honestly wouldn't have changed
anything for me.

1180
00:55:40,170 --> 00:55:41,671
I felt the flutter.

1181
00:55:43,590 --> 00:55:46,426
My voice is flat,
so it might not sound like I mean it.

1182
00:55:48,553 --> 00:55:50,180
But that's how I truly feel.

1183
00:55:52,098 --> 00:55:54,183
I wouldn't have asked you out today
